1
00:00:55,000 --> 00:00:59,000
"The Last Oath"

2
00:00:59,600 --> 00:01:04,100
(Episode 4: Immunogen)

3
00:01:11,500 --> 00:01:13,041
We just met by chance anyway.

4
00:01:14,458 --> 00:01:15,458
Ah, forget it.

5
00:01:29,208 --> 00:01:30,416
Lin Zai, you're awake.

6
00:01:30,750 --> 00:01:32,110
I'll go heat up some food for you.

7
00:01:32,291 --> 00:01:33,415
No need, Grandma.

8
00:01:33,416 --> 00:01:34,791
I'll just have some crackers.

9
00:01:40,291 --> 00:01:40,875
Sister Chen.

10
00:01:40,875 --> 00:01:41,458
Yeah?

11
00:01:41,458 --> 00:01:42,458
Where's A-Leh?

12
00:01:42,791 --> 00:01:43,791
He left.

13
00:01:44,708 --> 00:01:45,832
He left?

14
00:01:45,833 --> 00:01:47,166
Why didn't he tell me?

15
00:01:49,083 --> 00:01:50,000
Tell you what?

16
00:01:50,001 --> 00:01:51,321
Were you planning to go with him?

17
00:01:56,625 --> 00:02:00,125
It's hard to find a reliable
companion in this apocalypse.

18
00:02:00,750 --> 00:02:01,874
Man.

19
00:02:01,875 --> 00:02:03,541
If he wasn't in such a rush to leave,

20
00:02:04,125 --> 00:02:05,565
it would've been great if he stayed.

21
00:02:28,250 --> 00:02:30,416
Lin Zai, where are you going?

22
00:02:30,666 --> 00:02:31,958
I'm going to bring A-Leh back.

23
00:02:52,416 --> 00:02:53,616
Your injury hasn't healed yet.

24
00:02:53,750 --> 00:02:54,830
Why are you running around?

25
00:02:56,000 --> 00:02:57,000
You didn't leave.

26
00:02:59,041 --> 00:03:00,375
How did you guys get so dirty?

27
00:03:00,625 --> 00:03:01,625
Just our luck.

28
00:03:02,041 --> 00:03:04,208
We fell down a slope
while gathering firewood.

29
00:03:04,333 --> 00:03:05,708
Good thing it was a small one.

30
00:03:05,791 --> 00:03:07,711
Otherwise, we might not
have made it back today.

31
00:03:10,458 --> 00:03:11,250
Ugh.

32
00:03:11,251 --> 00:03:12,726
I feel like my mouth is full of dirt.

33
00:03:12,750 --> 00:03:13,375
Anyway,

34
00:03:13,376 --> 00:03:14,416
I need to go wash up.

35
00:03:29,083 --> 00:03:29,958
Hey!

36
00:03:29,958 --> 00:03:30,958
What are you doing?

37
00:03:31,041 --> 00:03:32,041
Put me down!

38
00:03:32,625 --> 00:03:33,625
Put me down!

39
00:03:42,666 --> 00:03:44,708
Hey, what's wrong with you two?

40
00:03:45,500 --> 00:03:46,540
His wound opened up again.

41
00:03:48,208 --> 00:03:49,790
What happened?

42
00:03:49,791 --> 00:03:51,916
They just went up the
mountain to gather firewood.

43
00:03:52,083 --> 00:03:53,791
Why did a wounded guy tag along?

44
00:03:56,291 --> 00:03:57,291
I thought...

45
00:04:03,291 --> 00:04:04,625
I... I'm fine now.

46
00:04:04,708 --> 00:04:05,708
It doesn't hurt anymore.

47
00:04:06,208 --> 00:04:07,625
Hey, Lin Zai.

48
00:04:07,958 --> 00:04:10,082
Wasn't your foot badly
injured a couple of days ago?

49
00:04:10,083 --> 00:04:11,416
It's almost healed now.

50
00:04:11,750 --> 00:04:12,750
Ah.

51
00:04:17,333 --> 00:04:18,333
Don't move.

52
00:04:24,208 --> 00:04:25,208
Oh.

53
00:04:26,625 --> 00:04:29,000
Maybe it just looked worse than it was.

54
00:04:32,208 --> 00:04:33,208
Yeah.

55
00:04:33,416 --> 00:04:35,416
It's great to be young.
You bounce right back.

56
00:04:43,625 --> 00:04:44,625
A-Leh.

57
00:04:45,166 --> 00:04:46,416
You should go wash up too.

58
00:04:48,958 --> 00:04:49,958
I'm on it.

59
00:05:00,458 --> 00:05:01,833
Don't go running around again.

60
00:05:24,583 --> 00:05:26,208
Immune target confirmed.

61
00:05:49,375 --> 00:05:50,375
Laundry detergent.

62
00:05:57,958 --> 00:05:59,250
The stains on your clothes,

63
00:05:59,750 --> 00:06:01,230
it's better to wash off what you can.

64
00:06:02,416 --> 00:06:03,416
No need.

65
00:06:03,666 --> 00:06:04,666
They're already dry.

66
00:06:08,458 --> 00:06:09,458
Alright.

67
00:06:13,750 --> 00:06:15,708
You never seem to get any real rest.

68
00:06:16,541 --> 00:06:17,750
Always on high alert.

69
00:06:17,875 --> 00:06:19,125
Aren't you tired?

70
00:06:20,291 --> 00:06:21,291
I'm used to it.

71
00:06:26,458 --> 00:06:27,458
A-Leh.

72
00:06:27,750 --> 00:06:29,166
What did you do before all this?

73
00:06:31,333 --> 00:06:33,333
The past isn't worth talking about.

74
00:06:36,583 --> 00:06:38,983
You mentioned before that you
had something important to do.

75
00:06:39,291 --> 00:06:40,291
What is it?

76
00:06:42,916 --> 00:06:44,500
That's none of your business.

77
00:06:51,583 --> 00:06:53,625
I thought we were friends.

78
00:06:54,666 --> 00:06:56,626
I just wanted to get to
know you a little better.

79
00:07:12,458 --> 00:07:13,582
I'm going to catch a couple of fish.

80
00:07:13,583 --> 00:07:14,663
We'll have a feast tonight.

81
00:08:04,000 --> 00:08:05,000
Hold out your hand.

82
00:08:11,583 --> 00:08:12,583
For you.

83
00:08:43,333 --> 00:08:44,333
A-Leh.

84
00:08:45,541 --> 00:08:47,166
I've lost a lot in this apocalypse.

85
00:08:48,083 --> 00:08:49,708
So I want to cherish the people I meet,

86
00:08:49,916 --> 00:08:51,375
the ones I can rely on.

87
00:08:53,500 --> 00:08:55,666
I think you're incredibly trustworthy.

88
00:09:00,708 --> 00:09:03,583
I think we could be
companions, like family.

89
00:09:06,708 --> 00:09:09,166
I don't know what you're
risking your life to do,

90
00:09:10,625 --> 00:09:11,958
but maybe we can help.

91
00:09:14,125 --> 00:09:15,125
That way,

92
00:09:16,125 --> 00:09:17,833
you won't have to struggle alone

93
00:09:18,541 --> 00:09:19,708
and get hurt so much.

94
00:09:38,250 --> 00:09:39,333
So,

95
00:09:39,833 --> 00:09:41,000
do you want to stay?

96
00:09:54,041 --> 00:09:55,083
No one can help me.

97
00:09:56,208 --> 00:09:57,208
I'm not staying.

98
00:10:02,750 --> 00:10:03,916
I understand.

99
00:10:05,041 --> 00:10:06,281
When are you planning to leave?

100
00:10:12,000 --> 00:10:13,125
Once your foot heals,

101
00:10:13,500 --> 00:10:14,500
I'll leave.

102
00:10:17,958 --> 00:10:19,558
You really don't need to worry about me.

103
00:10:19,625 --> 00:10:20,875
I'm pretty much healed.

104
00:10:21,500 --> 00:10:22,500
Look.

105
00:10:22,666 --> 00:10:24,226
I'm not even using my crutches anymore.

106
00:10:27,833 --> 00:10:28,833
Then I'll leave tomorrow.

107
00:11:01,083 --> 00:11:02,123
You're really not staying?

108
00:11:02,250 --> 00:11:03,250
My mind is made up.

109
00:11:12,458 --> 00:11:13,978
Those who are meant to stay will stay.

110
00:11:14,291 --> 00:11:16,958
You can't force someone
to stay if they want to leave.

111
00:11:17,791 --> 00:11:19,583
It's enough that our paths crossed.

112
00:11:25,791 --> 00:11:28,958
All good things must come to an end.

113
00:11:30,208 --> 00:11:31,208
A-Leh.

114
00:11:31,791 --> 00:11:33,332
No matter where you go,

115
00:11:33,333 --> 00:11:35,250
take care of yourself, okay?

116
00:11:37,083 --> 00:11:38,083
Thanks.

117
00:11:40,250 --> 00:11:41,250
Man,

118
00:11:42,125 --> 00:11:43,958
I really don't want you to go.

119
00:11:44,875 --> 00:11:46,250
If you stayed here,

120
00:11:47,208 --> 00:11:48,833
we'd feel so much safer.

121
00:11:49,791 --> 00:11:51,416
But since you've made up your mind,

122
00:11:52,750 --> 00:11:54,333
I won't say anything else.

123
00:11:58,875 --> 00:12:00,125
We're parting ways tomorrow,

124
00:12:00,583 --> 00:12:01,541
so let's treat this meal

125
00:12:01,542 --> 00:12:03,833
as a farewell party for A-Leh.

126
00:12:05,000 --> 00:12:07,166
Let's drink until we drop tonight!

127
00:12:07,583 --> 00:12:08,916
Come on, brother.

128
00:12:09,625 --> 00:12:10,625
Fill 'er up.

129
00:12:16,208 --> 00:12:17,208
Here.

130
00:12:18,875 --> 00:12:19,995
Your foot hasn't healed yet.

131
00:12:20,250 --> 00:12:21,250
You shouldn't drink.

132
00:12:21,750 --> 00:12:22,541
It's fine.

133
00:12:22,542 --> 00:12:24,166
Didn't you see my injury today?

134
00:12:24,791 --> 00:12:25,791
Besides,

135
00:12:27,166 --> 00:12:28,166
since we're friends now,

136
00:12:28,291 --> 00:12:29,291
I have to drink.

137
00:12:30,541 --> 00:12:31,625
Since you put it that way,

138
00:12:32,833 --> 00:12:33,833
fill it up.

139
00:12:36,458 --> 00:12:37,458
Come on.

140
00:12:40,333 --> 00:12:43,125
Here's to hoping we meet again someday.

141
00:12:45,541 --> 00:12:49,750
I hope every one of you
stays safe and healthy.

142
00:12:51,750 --> 00:12:55,708
I hope the zombie crisis ends soon.

143
00:12:58,958 --> 00:13:00,000
I hope...

144
00:13:02,416 --> 00:13:04,083
I hope all our wishes come true.

145
00:13:14,041 --> 00:13:15,083
Cheers!

146
00:14:20,208 --> 00:14:21,208
A-Leh.

147
00:14:22,416 --> 00:14:24,041
I've lost a lot in this apocalypse.

148
00:14:24,958 --> 00:14:26,583
So I want to cherish the people I meet,

149
00:14:26,791 --> 00:14:28,250
the ones I can rely on.

150
00:14:30,375 --> 00:14:32,541
I think you're incredibly trustworthy.

151
00:14:36,916 --> 00:14:37,916
So,

152
00:14:38,666 --> 00:14:39,791
do you want to stay?
